  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Physics within VRChat can be a bit rubbish for golf.


    Sometimes you
    may run into an issue like here below. This sand pit is a separate mesh to the
    rest of the course green. You might notice that rolling your ball over the seam
    bewteen the yellow/green, your ball pops up into the air for seemingly no reason.


    This
    is PhysX thinking that your ball sank into the edges between the 2 meshes and
    bounces your ball off it. Very annoying.


    The fix is to try and keep all
    of your meshes as one big collision mesh instead.

    Obviously this means you
    can''t use a different PhysicsMaterial for this part of the course!


    To
    get around this look at the sign to your left :)'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
